WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome, welcome, welcome.
Enjoy yourself.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.567
Have a good time.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:07.567
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching. Yeah!

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:11.567
Well, guys, everyone's talking
about this today.

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:13.133
Just minutes after liftoff,

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:17.734
Elon Musk's unmanned SpaceX
rocket exploded in midair.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.834
Yeah, at first, when people
saw the rocket light up

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:22.200
and start smoking,
they were like,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.868
"Alright, happy 4/20, everybody.
Yeah, we did it.

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:27.534
That's cool. Awesome, man."

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:30.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.834
Right after the
giant explosion,

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:34.534
Elon was like, "Crap, did we
launch a Tesla by mistake?"

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.834
Yeah, it took off fast,
was flying high,

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:41.534
and then all of a sudden
it exploded.

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:43.868
Kind of like Ron DeSantis'
presidential campaign.

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:49.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.033
Yeah, but SpaceX hopes
the rocket

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:54.634
will eventually be able
to take people to Mars.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:55.968
Yeah, and I think I speak
for everyone

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:57.567
when I say uh, you first.

00:00:57.567 --> 00:00:59.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.868
Mars, heaven.

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:02.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.968
Either way,
you're not coming back. Yeah.

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:06.701
That's right. The rocket
exploded minutes

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:09.701
into its flight, but SpaceX said
that they actually triggered

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:12.701
the explosion,
which is interesting.

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.801
But I think how they made
the rocket explode

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:16.467
is even more interesting.
Take a look at this.

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:29.300
There you go. That's it.
Mentos and Diet Coke.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.234
-That's how they did it?
-That's how they do it.

00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:34.033
-Wow. How viral.
-Interesting.

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.467
That's right.

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:37.868
SpaceX is now saying
they triggered the explosion,

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:39.167
but originally when it happened,

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:42.467
they called it a "rapid
unscheduled disassembly."

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:45.901
That sounds like
what celebrities say

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:47.968
when they're getting divorced.

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:50.934
Our marriage is going through a
rapid, unscheduled disassembly.

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:53.601
Please respect our privacy
at this time.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.667
That's right. SpaceX originally
described the explosion

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:58.400
as a rapid,
unscheduled disassembly.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.434
I don't know. It seems like they
were just trying to save face

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.234
instead of admitting
that it blew up.

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:03.868
-I don't think it's that weird.

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:06.367
They're just, you know,
classing it up a little bit.

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:07.601
-What do you mean?

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:09.534
-I mean, like,
instead of saying, "Jimmy,

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:12.133
I need tomorrow off,
I can say something like,

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.300
"You know, my body has plans
to be asleep

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.033
beyond my predetermined
alarm clock."

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:17.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:19.200
-It sounds like you're
dressing up the fact

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.634
that you're trying
to get out of work.

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:24.767
-No, no, it's more than that.
Instead of saying, "Jimmy,

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:26.767
I ate your lunch
out of the fridge,"

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:29.067
I'd say "my mouth
acquired a bread

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:30.968
and meat meal
from an unethical source."

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:32.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:35.100
-Just say you ate my sandwich.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.968
-Are you mad at me?

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:41.434
-I wouldn't say I'm mad.
I'd say my brain is consumed

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:43.534
with aggravated thoughts
towards my work peers.

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:45.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.067
-Hey, Jimmy, I want to do one.

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:48.534
-Go ahead, James.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:51.501
-My head smells weird because
I rubbed it against a wet dog.

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:56.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:57.901
-What does that mean?

00:02:57.901 --> 00:03:00.067
-It means my head smells weird

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:02.033
because I rubbed it
against a wet dog.

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:07.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:13.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:16.667
